@node math-test-functions Manual
@chapter Crate @code{math-test-functions}
@cindex math-test-functions
@cindex optimisation benchmark

@code{math-test-functions} is a curated library of 56+ non-linear
optimisation test functions used to benchmark @ref{math-optimisation
Manual} and to gate regressions in @code{just qa}.

@menu
* math-test-functions User Guide::
* math-test-functions Developer Guide::
@end menu

@node math-test-functions User Guide
@section User Guide

End users never call this crate. It is what gives us confidence that
the optimiser actually converges when the cost surface is hostile.

@node math-test-functions Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

@subheading Categories

@table @asis
@item Unimodal (convergence speed)
@code{sphere}, @code{rosenbrock}, @code{powell}, @code{dixons_price},
@code{zakharov}, @code{booth}, @code{matyas}, @code{sum_squares},
@code{elliptic}, @code{cigar}, @code{tablet}, @code{discus},
@code{ridge}, @code{sharp_ridge}, @code{brown}, @code{exponential}.
@item Multimodal (global search)
@code{ackley}, @code{rastrigin}, @code{griewank}, @code{schwefel},
@code{hartman_3d}, @code{hartman_4d}, @code{hartman_6d},
@code{michalewicz}, @code{alpine_n1}, @code{alpine_n2},
@code{branin}, @code{goldstein_price}, @code{six_hump_camel},
@code{eggholder}, @code{holder_table}, @code{cross_in_tray}.
@item Constrained
Selected non-linear constrained problems for COBYLA / SLSQP testing.
@end table

@subheading Usage

Each function exposes a uniform signature
(@code{Fn(&[f64]) -> f64}) and metadata (dimension, bounds, known
global minimum). Benchmarks in @code{math-optimisation} consume this
metadata to score solver runs automatically.

@subheading Visualisation

Interactive HTML plots live in @file{docs/interactive_plots.html}.

@subheading Testing

@example
cargo test -p math-test-functions
@end example
